WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
A small figure climbs
a steep zig-zag path.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.150
Mist hangs all around.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.350
Then the mist clears: a
huge glacier, and above it,

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.780
"the supreme and magnificent Mont Blanc".

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.070
The figure stops, tiny against the ice.

6
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.840
Victor is drowning in grief.

7
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.940
So why climb a glacier to feel better?

8
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.350
Why not sit by a quiet lake?

9
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.840
In this mission, you'll learn the difference
between the beautiful and the sublime:

10
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:33.210
calm pleasure, or awe mixed with terror.

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.540
You'll see how Edmund Burke
set out that contrast in 1757,

12
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.230
and why Romantic writers
went hunting for wild places.

13
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.860
And you'll ride with
Victor deep into the Alps,

14
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.010
through the ravine of Arve.

15
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.470
Your mission: explain why Victor
climbs a glacier to feel better.
